A('1963-02-caothang', '1963-02', VH, 'Saigon. The city\'s Commando Team 65 attacks the American billet at 31 Cao Thắng street, in February.', 'III, 293', when='Feb.', place='saigon', also=OP + ['vietnam'], check='the day.')
A('1963-0320-tsn', '1963-03-20', VH, 'Saigon. The Tân Sơn Nhứt airfield attacked, Mar. 20.', 'III, 293', place='tan-son-nhut', also=OP + ['vietnam'], check='the history gives the date and the target only; the American record not read.')
A('1963-0415-nghiahung', '1963-04-15', VH, 'Long Khánh. The night of Apr. 15, with the help of a man inside, the province\'s armed propaganda team enters the Nghĩa Hưng strategic hamlet: 13 pacification cadres and two Self-Defense men taken, 15 weapons, the watchtowers and fences torn down.', 'III, 296', place='long-khanh', band_='night', also=OP)
A('1963-0425-maag', '1963-04-25', VH, 'Saigon. The American military advisory office on Trần Hưng Đạo street attacked, Apr. 25.', 'III, 293', place='saigon', also=OP + ['vietnam'], check='the history gives the date and the target only; the American record not read.')
A('1963-0426-giavut', '1963-04-26', VH, 'Kon Tum. Sapper Battalion 409 and two companies of Battalion 95 (Regiment 2), under Regiment 2\'s chief of staff Hồ Văn Trí, ambush the guard of a Saigon engineer unit opening the road from Gia Vụt to Măng Đen, Apr. 26. Two hours: a battalion command, an infantry company and a platoon of artillery destroyed, two 105-mm guns taken.', 'III, 251', place='gia-vut', also=OP)
A('1963-0428-ducpho', '1963-04-28', VH, 'Quảng Ngãi. The night of Apr. 28 the people and troops of Đức Phổ district destroy most of the Saigon troops and administration in two communes, Phổ An and Phổ Quang, and the people rise.', 'III, 248', place='duc-pho', band_='night', also=OP, check='the history gives the night of Apr. 28 and a morning demonstration of Apr. 24; one date is a misprint.')
A('1963-0415-thiqua', '1963-04', VH, 'Mỹ Tho. Region 8\'s Battalion 261 attacks the Thị Qua bridge (Xóm Vuông) in mid-April: an infantry company and eight armored vehicles of the Saigon army destroyed.', 'III, 264', when='Apr., mid', place='thi-qua', also=OP, check='the day.')
A('1963-0504-mangxim', '1963-05-04', VH, 'Quảng Nam, Quảng Ngãi, Kon Tum. Saigon\'s II Corps, Gen. Nguyễn Khánh, sends three divisions against the Măng Xim base of Region 5\'s leaders, with two marine battalions to land in its center. The ground columns take their places in the "net" May 4. Regiment 2 and Battalion 409 with the local forces stop them; the marines landed at Nước Xu lose 80 men the same day; the reinforcing 22d Division convoy loses 13 vehicles at Cam Rẫy. May 15 the command ends the operation.', 'III, 250–52', to='1963-05-15', place='mang-xim', names=['Nguyễn Khánh'], also=OP, check='the history gives May 4 and May 15; the American record not read; the losses as the history gives them.')
A('1963-05-dakpet', '1963-05', VH, 'Kon Tum. A battalion of Region 5 fires 81-mm mortars by surprise on the Đắk Pét post in May, to back the local forces breaking strategic hamlets.', 'III, 245', when='May', place='dak-pet', also=OP, check='the day.')
A('1963-05-camson', '1963-05', VH, 'Mỹ Tho. Companies 1 and 2 of Battalion 514 besiege and destroy the Cẩm Sơn post in May and free two communes of Cai Lậy.', 'III, 265', when='May', place='cai-lay', also=OP, check='the day.')
A('1963-06-pleimrong', '1963-06', VH, 'Gia Lai. Battalions 200 and 407 move in secretly in June and attack the Plây Mơrông commando training camp, about 95 km northwest of Pleiku.', 'III, 246', when='June', place='plei-mrong', also=OP, check='the day.')
A('1963-0622-train', '1963-06-22', VH, 'Bình Thuận. The province\'s troops, with antitank mines made at the Cao Thắng engineering shop, wreck a 12-car train, June 22, and destroy all its arms and goods.', 'III, 261', place='binh-thuan', also=OP)
A('1963-0705-caimit', '1963-07-05', VH, 'Bến Tre. The province\'s troops with the guerrillas of Thạnh Phú Đông attack the Cái Mít post on the Hàm Luông, July 5.', 'III, 270', place='cai-mit', also=OP)
A('1963-0710-giongtrom', '1963-07-10', VH, 'Bến Tre. The secret cells of four communes, Thạnh Phú Đông, Hiệp Hưng, Tân Hào and Phước Long, bring 2,000 core supporters and soldiers\' families into Giồng Trôm town, July 10–15, to demand compensation for property and for husbands and sons killed, an end to sweeps and the sons\' return home.', 'III, 271', to='1963-07-15', place='giong-trom', also=['vietnam'])
A('1963-0709-baunau', '1963-07', VH, 'Tây Ninh. In early July a platoon of Company 33 of Gò Dầu with Cẩm Giang\'s guerrillas wipes out the Civil Guard platoon in the Bàu Nâu strategic hamlet and frees the people held in it.', 'III, 299', when='July, early', place='bau-nau', also=OP, check='the day.')
A('1963-0716-vung207', '1963-07-16', VH, 'Mỹ Tho. Battalions 261 and 514 and the district forces open the "July 20" campaign, the night of July 16, besieging the Cái Mít and Chợ Cầu posts. July 17–19 the 7th Division and M113s are held on the roads; the posts are abandoned July 19. The night of July 20 Battalion 261 destroys the Vĩnh Kim subsector; July 21, 15 posts in the area abandoned or surrendered. July 22 the command ends it: 12 communes of Cai Lậy and Châu Thành free, the "July 20 area".', 'III, 266–68', to='1963-07-22', place='vinh-kim', also=OP, band_='night', check='the first night\'s hour not given.')
A('1963-0720-onghan', '1963-07-20', VH, 'Mỹ Tho. 11:30 a.m., July 20. Saigon troops in several columns attack Company 2 of Battalion 514, assembled at the Ông Hàn bridge, Quảng Long; the position holds until dark and the company withdraws.', 'III, 267', place='ong-han', time='11:30', also=OP)
A('1963-0902-sonphu', '1963-09-02', VH, 'Bến Tre. Two main-force companies of the province with Giồng Trôm\'s district forces attack the Sơn Phú post, Sept. 2, and ambush Civil Guard Company 232 sent to relieve it', 'III, 271', place='son-phu', also=OP)
A('1963-0909-mynhon', '1963-09-09', VH, 'Bến Tre. The province\'s troops go down to Ba Tri with the district force and guerrillas and take the Mỹ Nhơn post, Sept. 9, then ambush and destroy Civil Guard Company 907, formed in French times.', 'III, 271', place='my-nhon', also=OP)
A('1963-0908-tantay', '1963-09-08', VH, 'Gò Công. The night of Sept. 8, Battalion 261 with the province\'s forces destroys the Tân Tây post and a Ranger company at the Gò Công subsector, then holds ground against the relief.', 'III, 273', place='tan-tay', band_='night', also=OP)
A('1963-0909-caiNuoc', '1963-09-09', VH, 'Cà Mau. The night of Sept. 9–10, Region 9\'s main-force Battalion 306 and the province\'s U Minh Battalion attack the subsectors of Cái Nước and Đầm Dơi, 21 km apart. At Cái Nước Battalion 306 is in position at 3:40 p.m., opens fire at 0:40 a.m. Sept. 10 and holds the subsector to 3 p.m. At Đầm Dơi the U Minh Battalion comes in 300 boats, in position at 6:30 p.m., fires at 4:10 a.m. and, on Nguyễn Đệ\'s order, withdraws by 6 a.m. Both subsectors destroyed, 327 out of action, among them the district chief and deputy of Đầm Dơi.', 'III, 286–89', to='1963-09-10', place='cai-nuoc', time='15:40', also=OP, extra='The time is the first day\'s, Battalion 306 in position at Cái Nước.', check='the figures as the history gives them; "one district chief killed, another taken" is cut off at III, 289.')
A('1963-09-khu8', '1963-09', VH, 'Region 8\'s committee holds a conference in mid-September to sum up the first phase of the "Emulate Ấp Bắc, kill the enemy, win merit, break the strategic hamlets" drive.', 'III, 276', when='Sept., mid', vis=True, tags=['ok:fields-place'], check='the day and the place.')
A('1963-09-gionglon', '1963-09', VH, 'Long An. Late in September, Đức Hòa\'s troops with the people attack the Giồng Lớn post, destroy a Civil Guard company and break the strategic hamlet there, after the provincial committee\'s conference of cadres on military attack with political struggle.', 'III, 277–78', when='Sept., late', place='long-an', also=OP, check='the day.')
A('1963-1018-caytruong', '1963-10-18', VH, 'Eastern Nam Bộ. Battalion 5 of Regiment 2, with a sapper company, attacks the Cây Trường post, Oct. 18.', 'III, 300', place='ben-cat', also=OP)
A('1963-1103-phumy', '1963-11-03', VH, 'Gia Định. The morning of Nov. 3 Battalion 514 destroys a unit under a man named Huề, takes the Phú Mỹ subsector and frees the communes of Phú Hòa, Tân Hòa Thành and Tân Lý Đông (Củ Chi).', 'III, 282', place='phu-my', band_='morning', also=OP, check='the history\'s "Phú Mỹ – Củ Chi" direction; the province of the subsector not given there.')
A('1963-1111-dakpet', '1963-11-11', VH, 'Kon Tum. The night of Nov. 11, after a mass fire raid by Battalion 200, the sappers of Battalion 407 attack the Đắk Pét base.', 'III, 246', place='dak-pet', band_='night', also=OP)
A('1963-1122-hiephoa', '1963-11-22', VH, 'Hậu Nghĩa. 1:00 to 1:40 a.m., Nov. 22. Long An\'s forces (two sapper companies, two infantry companies, an engineer platoon and Đức Hòa\'s district troops), under the province commander Huỳnh Công Thân, take the Hiệp Hòa commando training center on the Cambodian border corridor: 78 killed, nearly 100 prisoners, 500 weapons and about four tons of ammunition; two of the attackers killed.', 'III, 279', place='hiep-hoa', time='01:00', also=OP, names=['Huỳnh Công Thân'])
A('1963-1123-hiephoa2', '1963-11-23', VH, 'Hậu Nghĩa. Nov. 23 Saigon retakes the Hiệp Hòa base with a regiment, four helicopter gunships and 18 M113s in two columns, as thousands of people of four communes block the road and call on the soldiers to turn back.', 'III, 280', place='hiep-hoa', also=OP)
A('1963-1123-chala', '1963-11-23', VH, 'Cà Mau. The night of Nov. 23, under Nguyễn Hoài Phô, Region 9\'s Battalion 306, the U Minh Battalion, an antiaircraft battalion and local units attack the Chà Là strongpoint, 30 km southeast of Cà Mau town; Nov. 24 hundreds of the Saigon side out of action, hundreds of weapons and parachutes taken, 19 aircraft of all kinds shot down.', 'III, 290–91', place='cha-la', band_='night', names=['Nguyễn Hoài Phô'], also=OP, check='Nov. 24 is the history\'s day for the results.')
A('1963-1231-coptden', '1963-12-31', VH, 'Bến Cát. Dec. 31, Regiment 2 destroys Saigon\'s 32d Black Tiger Battalion of the 5th Division, advancing under American advisers into the area where the regiment sat holding its military-political conference: 250 out of action, 58 taken, three helicopters shot down, 110 weapons taken, by 6 p.m.', 'III, 302–03', place='ben-cat', also=OP, tags=['ok:fields-time'])
A('1963-1023-seatransfer', '1963-10', VH, 'The General Staff convenes a meeting in October with representatives of the Navy Department and Group 759 to carry out the transfer of sea transport to the navy.', 'III, 206', when='Oct.', place='hanoi', vis=True, check='the day.')
A('1963-0923-locan', '1963-09-23', VH, 'Haiphong. The night of Sept. 23 a wooden ship, Lê Văn Một master and Đặng Văn Thanh political officer, 12 men, leaves Bính Đông port to open a new landing at Lộc An, Bà Rịa, with arms for the Eastern Nam Bộ forces: north first to deceive watchers, then south, aground off Phước Hải a day and a night, in at Lộc An at dusk.', 'III, 205–06', place='haiphong', band_='night', tz='Asia/Bangkok', vis=True, also=OP + ['vietnam'], check='the day of arrival not given.')
A('1964-1026-logiao', '1964-10-26', VH, 'Bình Định. Ship 401, Phạm Vạn master, Đặng Văn Thanh political officer, 12 men, after turning back in a monsoon two weeks out, sails again Oct. 26 for Region 5. The night of Oct. 31 it goes aground in surf at the Lộ Giao landing; the arms are unloaded and hidden by dawn and the ship, badly damaged, secretly destroyed.', 'III, 209', to='1964-10-31', place='lo-giao', vis=True, also=OP + ['vietnam'], tags=['ok:fields-time'])
